How the art was made
--------------------
All of the art is AI-generated. Most of it was generated with OpenAI image models (through
ChatGPT and the Codex image tool) from prompts, many of which are stored beside the files in
the source tree (`*.prompt.txt`). The results were then selected, cropped, resized and
composed for the game. The full-size masters of several sets are in this repository beside
the files the game loads. `app/src/assets/PROVENANCE.md` lists, for each class of asset, how
it was made and where its prompts are; a few sets have no stored prompt. The icons, heraldry glyphs and seals are drawn as SVG by scripts in this
repository.

Because purely machine-generated images may not attract copyright in some jurisdictions, the
licence applies to the extent that rights exist.

The Niter, Oil and Silicon resource medallions in app/src/assets/resources/ were generated
with the Codex OpenAI image-generation tool on 2026-10-24 from the prompts beside the PNGs,
using the existing resource medallions as visual references. Selected variants were resized
for the game. They are included under the CC BY 4.0 terms above to the extent rights exist.

